 # Visualization mapping
 ## Overview
-Visualization mapping translates volumetric data values and derived features into optical properties and visual styles to resolve visual ambiguity in 3D datasets [G]. It determines which structures are visible, how they appear, and how users interact with the representation [G]. This family focuses exclusively on the mapping from data space to visual space, distinct from data representation [2-volume-data-and-representation.md](2-volume-data-and-representation.md) and rendering algorithms [16-image-order-rendering.md](16-image-order-rendering.md), [22-object-order-rendering.md](22-object-order-rendering.md). It operates on continuous volumetric samples rather than discrete isosurfaces [29-surface-extraction.md](29-surface-extraction.md), and prioritizes perceptual clarity and feature emphasis over strict physical accuracy [32-light-transport-in-participating-media.md](32-light-transport-in-participating-media.md).
